From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:53:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7000-mini4: Wake on the Smart Cover

Make the D2207 GPIO node the PMU event controller, as on the iPad 5 and
6. The PMU event line is SoC GPIO 107: Apple's device tree gives
/arm-io/i2c0/pmu "interrupts" 0x6b with flags 1 and interrupt-parent
/arm-io/gpio, on both the J96 and the J97, and the same flags on the
iPad 6 are its active-low line.

List the two Smart Cover hall sensors, GPIO 12 ("halleffect") and 10
("halleffect1"), as wake-only events 0x24 and 0x22, so that opening the
cover ends system sleep. While awake they stay polled.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi
index 87f1cd1..09952d1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi
@@ -235,6 +235,11 @@
 			/* Only REG_ON (3) is used; the others stay as iBoot left them. */
 			gpio-reserved-ranges = <0 3>, <4 6>, <11 1>, <13 8>;
 			/* Lines 10 and 12 are the Smart Cover hall sensors. */
+			interrupt-controller;
+			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+			interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl 107 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+			/* Smart Cover hall sensors (lines 10 and 12): wake only. */
+			apple,wake-events = <0x22 0x24>;
 		};
 	};
 };
